# Printed QR codes point at /go/<ref>. Astro builds a single /go/index.html, and these
# rewrites serve it for every campaign ref without a build step per campaign.
# Status 200 is a rewrite, not a redirect, so the ref stays in the URL and Cloudflare
# Web Analytics can group scans by it. The second rule covers a reload on
# /go/<ref>/<platform>, which the page itself writes via history.replaceState.
# Named placeholders rather than a splat: /go/* would also match the destination and
# Cloudflare rejects the rule as an infinite loop.
/go/:ref            /go/  200
/go/:ref/:platform  /go/  200
